00:04:58.235 --> 00:05:04.695
Surrey Local 1271 has a National Fund Raising Award, and the figure attached to this year's drive is $25,000.

00:05:05.315 --> 00:05:14.355
Fire and Safety Journal America says 60 firefighters raised that sum for muscular dystrophy Canada, pushing the local's lifetime giving to $266,000.

00:05:14.355 --> 00:05:20.115
The Surrey Firefighter's Charitable Society won the 2026 Dr. David Green Award for Fire

00:05:20.115 --> 00:05:23.315
Department of the Year to be handed over in Ottawa in November.

00:05:23.775 --> 00:05:28.875
The drive is a boot-tall, usually over a long weekend, at 20 commercial spots around Surrey.

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:33.435
President Mike Vincent said it hits home with members, who bring kids and families out,

00:05:33.775 --> 00:05:36.595
and that donations come easier once people see a firefighter.

00:05:37.035 --> 00:05:41.075
Member John Watkins said the work follows a promise made when they signed up, and that

00:05:41.075 --> 00:05:42.575
the award belongs to the membership.

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:48.475
The prize is named for neurologist David Green, who co-founded the charity in 1954 with Arthur

00:05:48.475 --> 00:05:48.795
Minden.

00:05:49.495 --> 00:05:53.815
Chief executive Stacey Linton said these firefighters lead by example and have pulled

00:05:53.815 --> 00:05:56.675
other British Columbia Union locals toward the same cause.

00:05:57.255 --> 00:06:01.735
Six District Vice President Mike Carter called the recognition a tremendous honor and a

00:06:01.735 --> 00:06:03.295
sign of what members can do locally.

00:06:03.755 --> 00:06:09.035
The same society delivers food to about 75 schools, give student bursaries, and has handed

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:11.035
out about 400 refurbished laptops.

00:06:11.035 --> 00:06:15.335
U.N. affiliates raised $1.1 million for the charity last year.

